# Local, opt-in semantic search index (#4339) — repo-local SQLite DB. Never
# committed; runtime code also refuses to write here if this entry is ever
# removed (see loom_tools.semantic_search.guard_index_dest_not_tracked).
.loom/search-index/

# NOTE (#7818): `.loom/gh-config/` and `.loom/gh-config-by-owner/` — the
# daemon-owned GH_CONFIG_DIR trees holding live GitHub App installation
# tokens (#4458/#5401) — used to be declared here by hand, which protected
# THIS repo only. They now live in EPHEMERAL_PATTERNS
# (loom-daemon/src/init/post_init.rs) and are emitted into the loom-managed
# block above, so every managed repo gets the rule. Do not re-add them here:
# one declaration site, enforced by scripts/check-gitignore-convergence.sh.

# Loom workspace config (DO commit for team sharing)
# - config.json: Persistent terminal configurations (roles, themes, intervals)
# - roles/: Custom role definitions

# One-off hand-made backups of config.json (e.g. `cp config.json
# config.json.bak-$(date +%Y%m%dT%H%M%SZ)`) — pure noise in git, which
# already keeps the full history; a leaked absolute host path in one such
# backup was an identity-class finding at HEAD (#6649). Never commit these.
.loom/config.json.bak-*

# Claude Code settings
# - settings.json: Team-wide permissions (DO commit)
# - settings.local.json: Personal preferences (gitignored)
.claude/settings.local.json

# Dogfood symlink (issue #3311):
# When loom is installed *on* the loom source repo, `.claude/agents` is a
# symlink to `defaults/.claude/agents/` so the in-repo agent definitions
# always reflect the committed source-of-truth (no copy = no drift).
# Created by `./scripts/install-loom.sh --dogfood .` or auto-detected when
# installing into the loom repo itself.
.claude/agents

# Dogfood scoped symlink (issue #3682, supersedes the #3565 copy):
# When loom is installed *on* the loom source repo, `.claude/commands/` is a
# real directory whose `loom/` subdir is a SYMLINK into the shipped source of
# truth: `.claude/commands/loom -> ../../defaults/.claude/commands/loom`.
# A symlink cannot go stale; the earlier materialized COPY (#3565) drifted
# whenever `defaults/.claude/commands/loom/*.md` changed and caused a false bug
# report (#3665) when agents loaded outdated guidance.
# Scoping the link to the `loom/` subdir (not the whole `.claude/commands`
# directory) avoids #3565's failure mode: `.claude/commands/` itself stays a
# real dir, so a co-installed tool writing a SIBLING namespace
# (`.claude/commands/<ns>/foo.md`, e.g. the `repo` tool) writes into a real
# dir and never redirects through a symlink into loom's `defaults/` artifact.
# No tool other than loom's own installer/daemon writes the `loom/` namespace.
# Established by `link_dogfood_commands` in scripts/install/dogfood-commands.sh
# (mirrors the `.claude/agents` handling, scoped one level deeper).
# IMPORTANT: this ignore lives ONLY in loom's own committed .gitignore.
# Consumer repos keep `.claude/commands/loom/` TRACKED (real files, not a
# symlink), so it must NOT be added to the daemon's `update_gitignore` list in
# loom-daemon/src/init/post_init.rs.
# Anchored with a leading `/`: an unanchored `.agents` also matches
# `defaults/.agents/`, silently ignoring every NEW shipped skill file.
.claude/commands

# Co-install hygiene (issue #3578, sibling of #3565):
# Loom ships no skills of its own (`defaults/.claude/skills/` does not exist),
# so `.claude/skills/` in the live tree is a pure destination for co-installed
# tools that write `.claude/skills/<ns>/…` (e.g. `repo` writes
# `.claude/skills/repo/SKILL.md`). Ignoring it keeps a foreign tool's files
# from being accidentally staged into loom's tree by `git add -A`.
# IMPORTANT: this ignore lives ONLY in loom's own committed .gitignore. It must
# NOT be added to the daemon's `update_gitignore` list in
# loom-daemon/src/init/post_init.rs, so consumer repos keep any skills they author TRACKED.
# If loom ever ships its own skills, materialize/dogfood them like
# `.claude/commands/loom/` (out of scope here).
.claude/skills

# Dogfood scoped symlink (issue #8947, fourth member of the #3311 /
# #3565+#3682 / #3578 family):
# `.agents/skills/` is the cross-vendor skill-discovery surface (#8673 contract
# point 5) that Codex, Kimi Code, Mistral Vibe and Grok read natively. When
# loom is installed *on* the loom source repo, `.agents/skills` is a SYMLINK to
# `../defaults/.agents/skills` — the shipped source of truth — so it cannot go
# stale the way #3565's materialized copy did before #3682 replaced it.
# Established by `link_dogfood_agent_skills` in
# loom-daemon/src/init/scaffolding.rs.
# IMPORTANT: this ignore lives ONLY in loom's own committed .gitignore.
# Consumer repos keep `.agents/skills/` TRACKED (real generated files, not a
# symlink — that is the whole point of shipping the surface), so it must NOT be
# added to the daemon's `update_gitignore` list in
# loom-daemon/src/init/post_init.rs.
# Anchored with a leading `/`: an unanchored `.agents` also matches
# `defaults/.agents/`, silently ignoring every NEW shipped skill file.
/.agents

# Skill routing local overrides (untracked, user-specific)
.loom/config/skill-routes.local.json

# Co-install hygiene, sibling of `.claude/skills` above: `.squad/` is a FOREIGN
# tool's runtime state directory (a SQLite database — `squad.db` plus its `-wal`
# / `-shm` companions). Loom neither writes nor reads it; it simply materializes
# in the checkout when that tool runs here. Left unignored it sits untracked and
# visible to this repo's documented `git add -A` Builder step, so a binary DB
# holding another tool's session state can be staged into a public remote.
# IMPORTANT: like `.claude/skills`, this lives ONLY in loom's own committed
# .gitignore — it must NOT be added to EPHEMERAL_PATTERNS in
# loom-daemon/src/init/post_init.rs, since consumer repos have no reason to
# inherit a rule for a tool they may not use.
.squad/

# NOTE (#8075): the host-local config override tier `.loom-local/` used to be
# ignored HERE, outside the managed block, which is precisely why consumer
# repos never got it — the installer-managed block is generated from
# EPHEMERAL_PATTERNS in loom-daemon/src/init/post_init.rs, not from this file.
# It now lives in that list (and therefore in the block above), with the
# rationale for ignoring it recorded alongside the pattern there.
